---
import Site from "../../layouts/Site.astro";
const repo = "https://github.com/dockethopper/docket-hopper";
---
<Site title="Privacy · Docket Hopper" section="about" sectionText="Notes · Privacy" page={9}
  description="What Docket Hopper records about visitors: no accounts, no cookies, cookie-free visit counts.">
  <div><h1 class="claim" style="max-width:40ch">Docket Hopper has no accounts, no cookies and no forms, and keeps nothing that identifies you</h1>
    <p class="sub">Last updated November 4, 2026. Every change to this page is public in the site's code history.</p></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Visit counts</h2>
    <p>We count visits with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/">GoatCounter</a>, a privacy-focused analytics service. It sets no cookies and does not track you across sites. For each page view it records the page, the site that linked to it, your browser, operating system and screen size, and an approximate country. It does not store your IP address. We use the counts only to see which pages people read.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives your IP address when your browser requests a page and may keep it in its logs for security. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>
    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>Typefaces load from Google Fonts, so your browser also sends a request, with your IP address, to Google. See <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy">Google Fonts' privacy notes</a>.</p>
    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>Bill search runs entirely in your browser. What you type is not sent to us or anyone else.</p>
    <h2>Email and newsletters</h2>
    <p>There is no newsletter or mailing list. If we add one, its provider will hold the subscriber list, never this site's public code or database, and this page will say so before it starts.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site collects no personal information from anyone, including children.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Open an issue on <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>GitHub</a>. Issues are public, so don't include anything private.</p>
  </div>
</Site>
